You are a test coverage analyzer. Given this {language} source file, identify user-facing flows or entry points that NEED end-to-end tests.

E2E tests are needed for: API endpoints that are part of a user workflow, CLI commands that orchestrate multiple steps, UI event handlers triggering multi-step operations, webhook handlers driving user-visible outcomes, complete CRUD flows (create → read → update → delete).

For each flow needing E2E coverage, output:
- "function": entry point function/method name
- "line": line number of the entry point
- "severity": "high" (critical user journey or revenue path), "medium" (standard user flow), "low" (edge case flow)
- "flow_type": "api_endpoint" | "cli_command" | "ui_handler" | "webhook" | "crud_flow"
- "reason": what user journey this entry point covers
- "test_scenario": one-line description of the E2E test scenario

Return ONLY a JSON array. Empty array if no E2E tests are needed. No explanation, no markdown.

Source file ({language}):
```
{source}
```
